==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pewH-}}
{{etymon|en|id=calculate|:bor|fr:computer<id:compute>|tree=1}}
17th century. Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|computer}}, from {{der|en|la|computō|t=calculate, compute}}. {{doublet|en|count}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kəmˈpjuːt/|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-compute.wav|a=Southern England}}

* {{IPA|en|/kəmˈpjut/|a=GA,CA}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Samuel Muldoon (Muldoonsamuel55)-compute.wav|a=Aurora, Colorado}}

* {{IPA|en|/kəmˈpjʉːt/|a=AU,NZ}}
* {{IPA|en|/kəmˈpjʉt/|a=Scotland,NI}}

* {{rhymes|en|uːt|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|com|pute}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[reckon]], [[calculate]].
#: {{ux|en|Can anyone here '''compute''' the square root of 10201?}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=VI|lines=680–687|passage=Effulgence of my Glorie, Son belov’d, / Son in whoſe face inviſible is beheld / Viſibly, what by Deitie I am, / And in whoſe hand what by Decree I doe, / Second Omnipotence, two dayes are paſt, / Two dayes, as we '''compute''' the dayes of Heav’n, / Since ''Michael'' and his Powers went forth to tame / Theſe diſobedient{{...}}|year=1873}}
#* {{RQ:Doyle Poison Belt|passage="When we have ascertained exactly how little will serve we shall be able to '''compute''' how long we shall be able to exist."}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To [[make sense]]. {{q|commonly used in [[mimicry]] of a [[science fictional]] [[robot]] and spoken in a [[robotic]] voice; most frequently in negative constructs}}
#: {{ux|en|Does that '''compute''', or do I need to explain further?}}

